From: SamuriHL <samurihl@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:20:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vdec: program the slave's stream write pointer on no-parser SoCs

On SoCs without a stream parser (S6) only the master of a dual-layer
stream-mode pair wrote HEVC_STREAM_WR_PTR / VLD_MEM_VIFIFO_WP; the slave
copied the master's wp into its own vbuf but left the register at the
value of the master's last run. Once the buffer drains to an access-unit
boundary the slave (Dolby Vision FEL enhancement layer) sees an empty
fifo, returns AGAIN forever, the dual scheduler keeps picking it, and the
master never runs again to refresh the register: decode stalls with the
buffer full (measured: EL hw WR_PTR frozen at be4d0ec7, vbuf wp bf23ce04).
---
diff --git a/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/utils/vdec.c b/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/utils/vdec.c
index 95deddf..59a76cd 100644
--- a/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/utils/vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/utils/vdec.c
@@ -2072,6 +2072,10 @@ static void vdec_sync_input_write(struct vdec_s *vdec)
 			} else {
 				STBUF_WRITE(&vdec->vbuf, set_wp,
 					STBUF_READ(&vdec->master->vbuf, get_wp));
+				/* the slave runs on the core too: without this it
+				 * decodes against the wp of the master's last run */
+				WRITE_VREG(VLD_MEM_VIFIFO_WP,
+					STBUF_READ(&vdec->vbuf, get_wp));
 			}
 		} else {
 			WRITE_VREG(VLD_MEM_VIFIFO_WP,
@@ -2085,6 +2089,10 @@ static void vdec_sync_input_write(struct vdec_s *vdec)
 			} else {
 				STBUF_WRITE(&vdec->vbuf, set_wp,
 					STBUF_READ(&vdec->master->vbuf, get_wp));
+				/* the slave runs on the core too: without this it
+				 * decodes against the wp of the master's last run */
+				WRITE_VREG(HEVC_STREAM_WR_PTR,
+					STBUF_READ(&vdec->vbuf, get_wp));
 			}
 		} else {
 			WRITE_VREG(HEVC_STREAM_WR_PTR,
